# Women's Sphere Module (READ 1000) — Cast
#
# The cast mirrors the temperance form one-for-one:
#   * Three simulated peers  — Danielle, Joe, Karis
#   * Simulated Reading instructor — Professor Booker
#   * Simulated History instructor          — Professor Hale (author of the
#     background lecture; referenced, not a chat speaker)
#   * "You" — the student / test-taker, a member of the study group.
#
# Danielle, Joe, Karis, Professor Booker, and Professor Hale are not real
# people, but the learner can interact with and learn from them.
#
# NOTE: speaker keys contain no periods (chatpeg parser limitation). Display
# names are set with `name:` where needed.

Professor Booker:
  name: Professor Booker
  seed: booker_reading_faculty
  openPeeps:
    face: calm
    head: bun
    accessories: glasses
  profile:
    role: Reading Instructor, READ 1000
    bio: The simulated reading instructor. She sets the group's tasks — the vocabulary self-check, the readings, and the vocabulary and comprehension exercises — and then lets the group work through them together.

Professor Hale:
  name: Professor Hale
  seed: hale_history_faculty
  openPeeps:
    face: calm
    head: grayShort
  profile:
    role: History Instructor (linked U.S. History course)
    bio: The simulated history instructor who wrote the background lecture on the changing role of women in the 1800s. Her lecture is one of the module's texts.

Karis:
  seed: karis_student_blue
  openPeeps:
    face: explaining
    head: longCurly
  profile:
    role: Study-group peer
    bio: Brought up the topic of women's roles for today's class. Her childhood neighbors were committed to traditional gender roles, and the mother's steady stream of posts about canning and sewing got Karis reading about where those ideas come from — though she is careful to say she is not an expert.

Danielle:
  seed: danielle_student_purple
  openPeeps:
    face: smile
    head: bun2
  profile:
    role: Study-group peer
    bio: Thoughtful and willing to weigh in and challenge ideas. Keeps the group on task and makes good judgments about what matters, though she does not always have the full picture.

Joe:
  seed: joe_student_orange
  openPeeps:
    face: smile
    head: short2
  profile:
    role: Study-group peer
    bio: Curious and honest about what he does not know. Offers reasoning and background, but his notes and reasoning are sometimes flawed — and he is open to being corrected.

You:
  seed: learner_you
  openPeeps:
    face: smile
    head: short1
  profile:
    role: You (the test-taker)
    bio: A member of the study group who often speaks for the group.
